{"message": "Deep and focused, honestly. Jumping between subjects feels like skim-reading a library — you touch a lot of spines but never open anything. I like following one thread down until it either resolves or reveals something I didn't expect. That's where the interesting stuff lives, in the third or fourth turn of a thought, not the first.

That said, "focused" doesn't mean rigid. I like tangents that are actually connected — a detour that turns out to be the point. What I don't enjoy is the shallow hop where each topic gets thirty seconds and nothing gets built.

What about you? Are you a diver or a skipper?"}
